{"id": "meal-contracts-under-the-line", "title": "Four pandemic meal contracts, each held just under $10 million before the Board saw them", "seconds": 130.6, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "a0e04041c334f042", "words": 408, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]"], "text": "A City contract of 10 million dollars or more needs a vote from the Board of Supervisors.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.37, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "The $10 million line", "sub": "at $10 million, the Board of Supervisors must vote"}, "emph": ["10 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.39, 0.85, 0.94, 1.12, 1.41, 1.76, 1.88, 2.3, 2.55, 2.62, 2.85, 3.01, 3.11, 3.32, 3.41]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "In 2020, the City hired four food vendors in a hurry. Where did each contract start?", "t0": 4.49, "t1": 9.75, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Pandemic meals, spring 2020", "sub": "under emergency authority"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.48, 1.02, 1.18, 1.44, 1.72, 1.95, 2.17, 2.52, 2.6, 2.67, 3.54, 3.76, 3.89, 4.06, 4.46]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "Each stood just under the line before the Board first saw it. Between 9.1 and 9.5 million.", "t0": 9.75, "t1": 15.4, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Before the Board’s first vote", "rows": [["SMG Food and Beverage", "9479817"], ["Off the Grid Services", "9405000"], ["Moonstar Buffet Restaurant", "9339000"], ["San Francisco New Deal", "9108000"]]}, "emph": ["just under"], "wt": [0.04, 0.28, 0.59, 0.84, 1.03, 1.14, 1.45, 1.72, 1.83, 2.08, 2.33, 2.58, 3.28, 3.67, 3.91, 4.16, 4.37, 4.5, 4.72, 4.97, 5.26]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 15.52, "t1": 17.15, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.29, 0.37, 0.94, 1.11, 1.18]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "The Board’s own resolutions give the amounts before and after every raise.", "t0": 17.37, "t1": 20.41, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "The Board’s own resolutions"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.09, 0.36, 0.5, 1.09, 1.25, 1.36, 1.68, 2.02, 2.14, 2.41, 2.64]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[0]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Moonstar actually began at 2,343,000 dollars.", "t0": 20.53, "t1": 23.74, "shot": "b4m", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Moonstar’s start, June 2020", "$2,343,000"], "b": ["after two agency raises", "$9,339,000"]}, "emph": ["2,343,000"], "wt": [0.0, 0.58, 0.95, 1.29, 1.37, 1.62, 1.86, 2.12, 2.35, 2.67]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[0]", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "The agency raised it twice, to 9,339,000.", "t0": 23.86, "t1": 26.63, "shot": "b4m", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Moonstar’s start, June 2020", "$2,343,000"], "b": ["after two agency raises", "$9,339,000"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.5, 0.74, 0.85, 1.38, 1.57, 1.79, 1.97, 2.18, 2.38]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "Who really paid? Not the City, mostly. The state capped meals at 66 dollars a person a day.", "t0": 26.75, "t1": 32.75, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "FEMA and the State", "sub": "pay back most of it"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Human Services Agency", "sub": "hires and pays vendors"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Older residents and hotel guests", "sub": "get the meals"}], "kicker": "Who pays"}, "emph": ["not the City"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.39, 1.36, 1.56, 1.68, 1.94, 3.01, 3.19, 3.55, 3.88, 4.22, 4.37, 4.95, 5.24, 5.31, 5.62, 5.69]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "Then federal and state money paid most of it back, through a program called Great Plates.", "t0": 32.87, "t1": 36.82, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "FEMA and the State", "sub": "pay back most of it"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Human Services Agency", "sub": "hires and pays vendors"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Older residents and hotel guests", "sub": "get the meals"}], "kicker": "Who pays"}, "emph": ["paid most of it back"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.48, 0.58, 0.87, 1.12, 1.33, 1.54, 1.63, 1.72, 2.32, 2.56, 2.62, 2.99, 3.2, 3.43]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "The first lead is those amounts. Four separate contracts, all within 9 percent under the line.", "t0": 37.04, "t1": 42.02, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Within 9 percent of the line", "kicker": "The first lead"}, "emph": ["9 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.39, 0.64, 0.76, 0.97, 1.91, 2.23, 2.52, 3.23, 3.48, 3.76, 3.95, 4.3, 4.5, 4.61]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[6]", "notEstablished[0]", "innocent[3]"], "text": "Why there? For two, the analyst printed the arithmetic: 1,500 people a day, at 60 dollars.", "t0": 42.14, "t1": 49.06, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "95 days at 1,500 people a day and a $60 meal rate, plus a 10 percent contingency"}, "emph": ["1,500 people a day"], "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 1.11, 1.31, 1.85, 2.02, 2.38, 2.71, 2.83, 3.98, 4.21, 4.62, 4.86, 5.09, 5.4, 5.46, 6.0, 6.15, 6.44]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[6]", "notEstablished[0]", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Plus 10 percent, over about three months. The records don’t say why those terms.", "t0": 49.18, "t1": 53.73, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "95 days at 1,500 people a day and a $60 meal rate, plus a 10 percent contingency"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.42, 1.28, 1.51, 1.73, 1.99, 2.74, 2.91, 3.24, 3.44, 3.6, 3.8, 4.02]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[7]"], "text": "A fifth meal contract, for shelters,", "t0": 53.85, "t1": 55.82, "shot": "b9f", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$9,917,050", "label": "a fifth contract: SF New Deal, meals in shelters", "sub": "raised by the Board to $18,990,675"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.36, 0.57, 1.07, 1.21]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[7]"], "text": "also began just under the line, at 9,917,050 dollars.", "t0": 55.82, "t1": 59.65, "shot": "b9f", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$9,917,050", "label": "a fifth contract: SF New Deal, meals in shelters", "sub": "raised by the Board to $18,990,675"}, "emph": ["9,917,050"], "wt": [0.04, 0.39, 0.7, 0.96, 1.16, 1.27, 1.84, 2.01, 2.26, 2.51, 2.79, 3.0, 3.3]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "The second lead: every one was then raised past the line. To how much, all together?", "t0": 59.87, "t1": 65.7, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Then raised", "kicker": "The second lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.42, 1.27, 1.61, 1.78, 1.93, 2.39, 2.76, 3.05, 3.18, 3.95, 4.14, 4.31, 4.64, 4.85]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "amount"], "text": "120.2 million dollars.", "t0": 65.7, "t1": 67.85, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$120.2 million", "label": "combined ceiling after amendments", "sub": "3.2 times the $37.3 million before the Board’s first votes"}, "emph": ["120.2"], "wt": [0.04, 0.24, 0.56, 0.88, 1.13, 1.34, 1.62]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "So the Board did vote, later, once the vendors were chosen and the work under way.", "t0": 68.37, "t1": 72.05, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the Board’s review was postponed rather than avoided"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.28, 0.54, 0.71, 1.01, 1.51, 1.75, 1.85, 2.16, 2.29, 2.72, 2.84, 2.94, 3.17, 3.39]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[1]"], "text": "The third lead: two of those votes were retroactive. That means approving terms already begun.", "t0": 72.27, "t1": 77.4, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Approved retroactively", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "files 201214 and 210415"}, "emph": ["retroactive"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.4, 0.97, 1.19, 1.28, 1.49, 1.75, 1.92, 3.2, 3.43, 3.65, 4.06, 4.38, 4.66]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "Moonstar’s contract began in June 2020. Its raise reached the Board in April 2021.", "t0": 77.52, "t1": 82.77, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2020-06-22", "to": "2021-04-27", "days": "309", "fromLab": "Moonstar contract began", "toLab": "amendment introduced", "kicker": "The third lead"}, "emph": ["April 2021"], "wt": [0.0, 0.55, 1.03, 1.34, 1.46, 1.69, 1.96, 2.75, 2.99, 3.25, 3.47, 3.57, 3.84, 3.95, 4.38, 4.69]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "The fourth lead: no price competition. The vendors came from lists of qualified firms, under emergency rules.", "t0": 82.99, "t1": 89.17, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Chapter 21 emergency procurement", "kicker": "The fourth lead"}, "emph": ["no price competition"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.41, 1.12, 1.34, 1.64, 2.92, 3.08, 3.41, 3.63, 3.82, 4.05, 4.14, 4.63, 5.02, 5.26, 5.73]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[5]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "93 vendors qualified for Great Plates, and 31 organizations applied for shelter meals.", "t0": 89.29, "t1": 94.11, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["pre-qualified vendors, Great Plates", "93"], "b": ["organizations on the shelter-meals list", "31"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.57, 0.98, 1.46, 1.6, 1.81, 2.5, 2.66, 3.09, 3.71, 4.0, 4.11, 4.44]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "A list shows who could do the work, not who offered the best price.", "t0": 94.23, "t1": 97.94, "shot": "b16q", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "A qualifications list shows who was able to do the work, not who offered the best price."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.39, 0.84, 1.08, 1.24, 1.37, 1.47, 2.15, 2.46, 2.65, 2.93, 3.03, 3.24]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[4]", "story[4]"], "text": "FEMA, the federal emergency agency, approved 61.3 million dollars of meal costs.", "t0": 98.16, "t1": 103.09, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "What FEMA approved", "kicker": "The federal bill", "chip": "$61,293,197"}, "emph": ["61.3 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.54, 0.69, 1.04, 1.53, 1.99, 2.37, 2.94, 3.21, 3.49, 3.8, 4.1, 4.21, 4.42]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[3]"], "text": "And what were the three Great Plates contracts paid?", "t0": 103.21, "t1": 105.82, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Paid under the Great Plates contracts", "kicker": "The federal bill"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.27, 0.41, 0.53, 0.83, 1.06, 1.39, 1.85]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[3]", "story[4]"], "text": "61.1 million dollars.", "t0": 105.82, "t1": 107.66, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$61,059,832", "label": "paid under the three Great Plates contracts", "sub": "$233,365 less than FEMA approved"}, "emph": ["61.1"], "wt": [0.04, 0.57, 0.85, 1.05, 1.35]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[3]", "established[4]", "story[4]"], "text": "That’s 233,365 dollars less than FEMA approved.", "t0": 108.18, "t1": 113.06, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["paid under Great Plates", "$61,059,832"], "b": ["costs FEMA approved", "$61,293,197"]}, "emph": ["less"], "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.48, 0.75, 1.24, 1.82, 2.16, 2.49, 3.18, 3.57, 3.8, 3.97, 4.32]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "established[8]", "notEstablished[4]"], "text": "The records don’t show anyone set the amounts to dodge the Board. Or that meals went undelivered.", "t0": 113.28, "t1": 118.01, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That anyone sized contracts to avoid the Board", "That meals were not delivered or were overbilled", "Whether the kitchens were inspected: 70 inspections citywide, April to June 2020"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.55, 0.76, 1.01, 1.41, 1.59, 1.69, 2.05, 2.19, 2.47, 2.57, 3.27, 3.44, 3.61, 3.91, 4.13]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The cost estimate behind each start amount. And meal counts per vendor.", "t0": 118.13, "t1": 123.03, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The cost estimate behind each start amount"}, {"who": "", "what": "Meals per vendor per month"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.26, 0.55, 1.36, 1.52, 1.84, 2.21, 2.5, 2.67, 2.94, 3.58, 3.82, 4.05, 4.36, 4.51]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "No audit or finding was found. The Board approved every raise, two after the fact.", "t0": 123.15, "t1": 127.57, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.56, 0.7, 1.09, 1.24, 2.11, 2.27, 2.48, 2.83, 3.07, 3.37, 3.65, 3.9, 4.0]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 127.69, "t1": 129.66, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.35, 0.45, 0.52, 1.06, 1.26, 1.35]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "found": "On the record", "lead1": "Lead 1 · just under the line", "lead2": "Lead 2 · raised past it", "lead3": "Lead 3 · after the fact", "lead4": "Lead 4 · lists, not prices", "lead5": "The federal bill", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "flow", "hook": "number"}